Error [jet.ComptimeValueIsRuntimeHandle]: `ct` is computed while building, but its value is a `Reader`, a runtime handle with no data form
  --> tests/ui/comptime_dependency_handle_value.jet:5:5
    |
  5 |     ct: #run Reader.over([U8]{7, 9, 11})
    |     ^^
 Why: A compile-time value must be data, which the build keeps and hands to later compile-time code and to the program. A runtime handle such as a `Reader` lives only in the run that made it.
 Fix: Use the `Reader` inside one `#run`, such as a function it calls, and keep only the data that work returns.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E1018
